SUMMARY:Hunters Camp to Creekside Connector Loop - Occidental
DESCRIPTION:Mindfull Hikes\n***Please be in good enough shape to hike at a
  moderate/fast steady pace (+/-2.5 mph) and comfortable with elevation cha
 nges.***\n\n**Distance:** +/- 5.6 miles total\n\n**The hike:** A lollipop 
 loop near Occidental. Generally considered a moderately challenging route\
 , with 900 ft. of elevation gain. From the trailhead the hike begins by de
 scending down an old logging road. We'll then follow a trail until our res
 t area near the creek with a few simple benches.\nLots of Redwoods along t
 he way! We'll take a trail back to the logging road/Hunters Camp trail and
  ascend back up to the trailhead. Note...the second half is a steady climb
  back up to the trailhead. This is a popular trail for hiking\, mountain b
 iking\, and running.\n\n**Parking:** is limited\; Carpool if you can.\n\n*
 *Where to meet:** Coleman Valley Road at the gate at the trailhead. Please
  note that if you use the address instead of the pin for navigation it tak
 es you past the meeting point\; you'll know because there is a private pro
 perty sign and no cars at that gate\; turn around and come back toward Occ
 idental about 1/3 mile.\n\n*Please be on time. We’ll start promptly at t
 he start time listed.* Give yourself a little extra time to arrive and get
  situated so that you’re part of the opening circle as this is an essent
 ial part of our time together.\n\nNo restroom available\n\n**What to bring
 :** Snack\, water\, hat\, good hiking shoes\, a joyful spirit and laughter
 . Please dress appropriately for the weather that day. Layers of clothing 
 are always advisable.\n**===================================**\n**Reminder
 s:**\nMindful hikes are intended to be a way to connect more fully with ou
 rselves\, each other and with the land. There will be two periods of silen
 t walking throughout the hike to allow the senses to be fully alive and fe
 lt. There will also be time during the hike to visit and connect with each
  other. These times of talking and connecting are an invitation to bring m
 indfulness to the present moment. **It's a time to put away the cell phone
  and cameras to disengage from technology to be fully present with each ot
 her\, our *senses and the land we are inhabiting.***\n\n***If you're on th
 e waitlist for the hike and want to attend please message Vickie a few day
 s before the scheduled hike. Most hikes have people drop off at the last m
 inute and it's possible there is an opening.***\n\n**Dāna**\nIn the spiri
 t of the Buddhist tradition mindful hikes are offered as a dāna based eve
 nt. Rick Hansen says “generosity is a beautiful practice that opens and 
 gladdens the heart\, relaxes the contraction of ‘self’ and ripples out
  into the world to touch many people.” The dāna practice is **heart cen
 tered** and in the spirit of generosity. Venmo or cash is graciously accep
 ted. Venmo account is: @vickieix8\; last four digits 4714 of my phone # if
  asked.\n\n**No-Show Policy:** Please cancel at least 24 hours before the 
 start of the hike. Be mindful that there may be a waitlist. If your plans 
 change and you're not coming\, opening up a spot 4-5 days before the hike 
 it's more likely someone will be able to attend than if you cancel at the 
 last minute. You're considered a no-show if you cancel at the last minute.
  Members with 2 no-shows will be removed from the group.
